# 1. Two Sum (LeetCode - Easy)

### My Approach :
1. Is problem ko fast ($O(n)$ time) solve karne ke liye maine ek HashMap use kiya hai, jisme hum har number aur uska index store karte hain.
2. Array par loop chalate waqt, har current number (`exactnum`) ke liye hum check karte hain ki `target - exactnum` (yaani `requiredNum`) pehle se map mein hai ya nahi.
3. Agar `requiredNum` map mein mil jata hai, toh iska matlab humein dono numbers mil gaye hain, aur hum unke indices return kar dete hain.
4. Agar nahi milta, toh hum current number aur uske index ko map mein add kar dete hain taaki aage aane wale numbers ke saath match kiya ja sake.


### Kotlin Code:
```kotlin
import java.util.HashMap

class Solution {
    fun twoSum(nums: IntArray, target: Int): IntArray {
        val map = HashMap<Int, Int>()
        
        for (i in nums.indices) {
            val exactnum = nums[i]
            val requiredNum = target - exactnum
            
            if (map.containsKey(requiredNum)) {
                return intArrayOf(map[requiredNum]!!, i)
            }
            
            map[exactnum] = i
        }
        
        return intArrayOf()
    }
}
```
